# /etc/default/llama-server — AgentX llama.cpp router service configuration.
#
# Installed once by `make llamacpp-service-install` and never overwritten on
# reinstall (same non-clobbering convention as `make seed` uses for AgentX's
# own agentx.toml) — edit this file directly to change settings, then:
#   sudo systemctl restart llama-server
#
# The LLAMA_ARG_* variables below are llama.cpp's OWN native environment
# equivalents for its `llama serve` CLI flags (run `llama serve --help` and
# look for the "(env: ...)" annotations) — not an AgentX invention, so this
# file stays in sync with upstream without any translation layer in
# scripts/llama-server.

# A `cmake --install` destination — i.e. a directory with the `llama` binary
# under bin/ and its shared libraries under lib/, NOT a raw build tree (those
# colocate both in one dir and rely on a build-tree RPATH a real install
# strips). `make llamacpp-install`'s LLAMACPP_INSTALL_PREFIX (default
# /opt/llama.cpp) is exactly this path — that target prints it on success.
LLAMACPP_PREFIX=/opt/llama.cpp

# Directory the router scans for GGUF models. `make llamacpp-models-dir`'s
# LLAMACPP_MODELS_DIR (default /opt/llama-server/models) is exactly this
# path — deliberately not under a user's home directory, since a home dir's
# own permissions commonly block traversal for a service account no matter
# how open the models dir itself is; /opt is world-traversable by default.
LLAMA_ARG_MODELS_DIR=/opt/llama-server/models

# Optional: per-model launch flags (context length, GPU layers, etc), INI
# format (llama.cpp's --models-preset). Comment out entirely to omit the
# flag — an empty value is not the same as unset for some llama.cpp flags.
#LLAMA_ARG_MODELS_PRESET=/opt/llama-server/models/preset.ini

# Must match [agentx.llamacpp] host in agentx.toml for AgentX to find this
# server.
LLAMA_ARG_HOST=0.0.0.0
LLAMA_ARG_PORT=8888

# Optional: any other `llama serve` flag not covered above, appended
# verbatim (space-separated) — e.g. "--ctx-size 8192 --n-gpu-layers 99".
LLAMACPP_EXTRA_ARGS=
